{"actor_ref":"claude","class":"draft_history","document_uuid":"01a1a54a-30ea-710d-80d5-ff9fc15961ba","id":"01a1a586-6308-70b9-9f77-dddba998e2c1","idempotency_key":"5ff983f5066bee32f8ffab3b1488969d2e24e890044f538629b34a670bd6827c","occurred_at":"2026-11-04T07:46:50Z","payload":{"note":"crates/ai/src/board.rs (feature host). BoardContent models moves/annotations/arrows/circles/notes_md/metadata and keeps unmodelled fields verbatim through serde(flatten), so a newer client's tree/clock survive a tool write; empty sections are omitted so stored JSON stays {\"moves\":[\"e4\"]}. BoardWriteHost implements ToolHost over rbc_db::Db with an actor name for the revision log: play_move replays the board's own move list from start_fen with shakmaty and accepts SAN or UCI, returning applied+san+fen+plies, illegal without touching the row; draw_arrow/draw_circle replace the same shape, clear_shapes empties both, annotate upserts by ply and sorts, write_note replaces notes_md; create_board/copy_board go through the repository (copy records copied_from/copied_revision); lock_board/unlock_board use set_board_mutability; get_board/list_boards/list_studies/get_study/create_study read and write through the same boundary. BoardWriteError maps to conflict (data.current_revision), copy_required, not_found and internal, every write carrying expected_revision. Evidence: cargo test -p rbc-ai --all-features write_tools -> 17 tests (SAN and UCI moves, whole lines, illegal move leaves revision 1, conflict reports revision 2 and keeps the other write, locked board asks for a copy, shapes replace and clear, which-correction, unknown content fields preserved, provenance, lock/unlock, unknown board and tool, study draft). Server still checks clean.","target":"t-4eb3"},"type":"work.note_added","v":2}
